{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dn51wfiLxrD5YJeM195oa6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"0731e41bea875494f9532b3ce882f7989f05ce07","date":"2026-10-06T15:24:43+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6044: Provide WHO z-score reference data to the Angular form engine (#3753)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-6044: Provide WHO z-score reference data to the Angular form engine\n\nesm-form-entry-app now registers the WHO reference data that the\nngx-formentry z-score helpers expect, so forms that calculate growth\nz-scores can be saved.\n\nThe helpers take the reference data as their first argument, e.g.\ncalcWeightForHeightZscore(weightForHeightRef, height, weight). The app\nnever registered weightForHeightRef, heightForAgeRef or bmiForAgeRef, so\nthese expressions failed as soon as a height or weight was entered. When\nan expression fails, the expression runner sets the field to false, and\nthe backend rejects false as the value of a numeric obs.\n\nwireDataSources now registers each reference the form schema mentions,\nwith the data for the patient's sex and age, chosen the same way as\nAMPATH's ng2-amrs. A reference that doesn't apply to the patient is\nregistered as null, which the helpers handle. The eight tables are\ncopied from esm-form-engine-lib and are identical to ng2-amrs's copies.\nEach one is a dynamic import, so forms that don't use the references\ndon't download them, and forms that do load at most two tables.\n\n* Use WHO's girls' height-for-age data and cover the month after age 5\n\nhfa_girls_5_above.json was a copy of the boys' table, so girls aged 5 to\n17 got height-for-age z-scores against boys' heights. It's now generated\nfrom WHO's Growth Reference 2007 girls' height-for-age z-score tables.\nEach column is M * (1 + k * S), rounded half to even to three decimals.\nThe same method regenerates hfa_boys_5_above.json byte for byte from\nWHO's boys' tables.\n\nThe loader switched to the 5 to 19 year tables on the fifth birthday,\nbut those start at 61 months, so height-for-age and BMI-for-age had no\nreference for a month. Height-for-age now uses the under-5 table through\nday 1,856, where that table ends, and the 5 to 19 year table from month\n61 after that. BMI-for-age has no under-5 table, so it has no reference\nuntil the 5 to 19 year table starts.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6ce8da22e588bfb7ee479298811f2bb4a064e2be","date":"2026-10-06T13:18:13+03:00","message":"(chore) O3-6025: Add missing form engine translation keys (#3754)","refs":"","body":"Adds the translation keys that the patient chart's form engine lib build\nuses but that weren't in esm-form-engine-app's key list, so they're\nextracted to en.json and can be translated. Until now these strings\nshowed in English in every locale.\n\nThree come from openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib#824, for the error shown when\na form's data fails to load: errorLoadingFormDependencies,\nretryLoadingFormDependencies and retry.\n\nThe other eight were added to the lib earlier and never listed: the\n\"Form submitted\" and \"Record updated\" toasts (submittedForm,\nsubmittedFormDescription, updatedRecord, updatedRecordDescription), the\nform submission error (errorProcessingFormSubmission), the mark-deceased\naction error (errorMarkingAsDeceased), and person attribute saving\n(personAttributesSaved, errorSavingPersonAttributes).\n\nen.json is regenerated with extract-translations. Every static t() key in\nthe lib build (4.2.2-pre.2663) is now in en.json.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"715ec982cb5008f64cf590e3335001b4de19843e","date":"2026-09-29T22:25:43+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry\n\nSave lab results and discontinue the test order in a single encounter\nrequest, then mark the order as fulfilled. The backend saves inline\norders inside the same transaction as the obs, so a failed discontinue\nno longer leaves the results saved behind it.\n\nPreviously the results, the discontinue and the fulfiller update were\nthree separate requests. If a later one failed, the results were already\nsaved, the order was not COMPLETED, and the form stayed in create mode.\nRetrying posted the obs to the encounter again. If the fulfiller update\nwas the one that failed, every retry added another copy and then failed\non the discontinue, because the backend rejects stopping an order twice.\n\nWhen an order already has saved results but is not COMPLETED, the form\nnow fills in the saved values and saving updates those obs. It then\ndiscontinues the order only if it is still active and marks it as\nfulfilled. A failed save refetches the saved results so the next attempt\nsees them.\n\n* Check for saved results when the user saves\n\nDecide whether to create or update results from a fresh fetch of the\norder's encounter at submit time, instead of the results the form loaded\nearlier. After a failed attempt, the form refetches its results in the\nbackground, and Save is available again before that refetch finishes.\nA quick retry in that window used to take the create path again. If the\nfetch fails, nothing is saved.\n\n* Keep the user's edits when saved results load\n\nOnly fill in saved result values for fields the user hasn't changed.\nAfter a failed save, the form refetches the saved results, and if the\nuser corrected a value while that was in flight, the refetched value\nreplaced their correction.\n\n* test: verify lab result edits are saved after delayed refresh\n\nExtend the delayed-results regression test through Save and close. Check that the corrected value is submitted, the workspace closes, and the success message is shown.\n\n* Cover failed lab result updates on retry\n\nCheck that a failed result update keeps the workspace open and stops the order from being completed. Update the refetch comment to describe how it fills in saved values.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"dd5d6a1d101e2647496fa4e5218ac4b7381d661c","date":"2026-09-25T06:53:36-04:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove support for offline from patient-chart (#3689)","refs":"","body":"Remove offline form submission, synchronization handlers, and offline visit helpers in preparation for removing offline support from the framework. Remove the related configuration, routes, and unused imports. This removes the offline visit API exported by patient-common-lib.","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"385d75cc2bbcc2a6802ca4f96dde611072cd4dec","date":"2026-09-17T21:05:49+03:00","message":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)","refs":"","body":"* fix: preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls\n\nTrack image additions and removals as form changes and read the current images for each upload callback so batches retain every file. Use labelled, contrasting remove buttons that do not submit the form. Cover create and edit workflows, batch uploads and removal.\n\n* fix: preserve image remove button contrast across interaction states\n\nSet explicit hover, focus and active colours so Carbon secondary button styles cannot hide the close icon. Remove the redundant button type, which Carbon already defaults to button.\n\n* fix: identify images in visit note removal labels\n\nUse the image description, filename or image number in each remove button's accessible name. Update the translation and tests to cover the fallbacks and select the intended image by name.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b147fb5906f1c3df18f12e3c804daeea486813d2","date":"2026-06-22T16:41:48+05:30","message":"(fix) Attach visit to visit note submissions (#3406)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"6797e139e35959962c51b4148213d88ccdc94af7","date":"2026-05-26T19:38:03+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5077: Support recording clinical procedures (#3320)","refs":"","body":"* Update pull request branches in CI workflow\n\nRemove main branch restriction from pull requests.\n\n* Remove 'patch/*' branch from CI trigger\n\n* Update CI workflow to include additional branches\n\n* Add esm-patient-procedures-app to patient-chart monorepo\n\n* Refactor the file structure\n\n* Add feat/procedure-history branch to workflow triggers\n\n* Modify E2E test triggers for additional branches\n\nUpdated branch filters for E2E tests on push and pull request events.\n\n* Make concept sources configurable\n\n* Load durations dynamically\n\n* Make the form wider\n\n* Make the duration unit combo box\n\n* Make status a combo box\n\n* (fix) O3-5656: Make submit buttons sticky on procedure history form (#3290)\n\n* Fix: stick the submit buttons in procedure form\n\n* Fix: update procedures-form.workspace.test.tsx to new ComboBox components\n\n* (fix) O3-5657: Various fixes to the procedures form (#3297)\n\n* (fix) O3-5653: Wire body site and status concepts in config schema (#3313)\n\n\n\nCo-authored-by: Jayasanka Weerasinghe <33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Cleanup the file structure\n\n* Migrate to vitest\n\n* Fix the workspace\n\n* Isolate date time component\n\n* Prevent future 'any' types\n\n* Convert all function declarations to arrow functions\n\n* Fix accessibility issues in ConceptSearchField (#15)\n\n* Clear slected concep when changing value\n\n* Re-enable delete button after failed delete\n\nsetIsDeleting(false) was missing from the catch block, leaving\nthe Delete button permanently disabled after a transient error.\nUser had to close and reopen the modal to retry.\n\nAlso updates the test assertion to verify the button is re-enabled\nafter an error so the user can retry without reopening the modal.\n\n* docs: add README for esm-patient-procedures-app\n\n* Add README for esm-patient-procedures-app\n\n* Rename file\n\n* Enable delete button on error\n\n* Rename file\n\n* Add separate pagination configs for overview and detailed view\n\n* Align import order and type placement with O3 coding conventions\n\n* Add unit tests for ConceptSearchField and ProceduresActionMenu (#21)\n\n* Add test cases for procedures form component\n\n* Rename close workspace\n\n* Add translations to zod schema\n\n* Minor cleanups\n\n* Reset workflows\n\n* Remove unused abort controller\n\n* Update routes\n\n* Fix the overvierw URL\n\n* Add backend dependancies\n\n* fix: convert type-only imports to 'import type' syntax in procedures-app\n\nConvert all type-only imports in the procedures-app package to use\nthe 'import type' syntax instead of inline 'type' prefixes. This\nimproves code consistency and clarity.\n\nUpdated files:\n- procedures.resource.ts\n- dashboard.meta.ts\n- components/**/*.tsx\n- workspaces/procedures-form/**/*.tsx\n\nAddressed in PR #3320 review comment.\n\n* Remove selectedConcept from hook, use RHF as UUID source of truth\n\n* Surface hook errors in the UI\n\n* Address remaining PR review comments from denniskigen\n\n* Set date boundaries\n\n* Update config descriptions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dilan Kavishka <109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","authorEmail":"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2c514a99a75389e9ccf680a9584eb68db57a2267","date":"2026-04-21T16:48:02+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5618: Validate condition selection before submit triggers (#3240)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Om Srivastava","authorEmail":"79087911+omsrivastava512@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d4857fbf84af21943b989c91c1b37277ff3ff2fd","date":"2026-04-17T16:01:13+03:00","message":"(feat) Surface BMI reference ranges in the biometrics table (#3238)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1ea865ec269e781482352f0307b124b2b78443aa","date":"2026-03-23T22:39:28+03:00","message":"(fix) Return promises from onSubmit handlers to track isSubmitting (#3158)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"05fb7434b9c74c51773439a5f94580ab7651b91d","date":"2026-03-23T23:22:32+05:30","message":"(fix) Prevent duplicate encounter creation on repeated submit (#3156)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Om Srivastava","authorEmail":"79087911+omsrivastava512@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"3e58d3eb4e079c4d530e105dcd963f034e4f9271","date":"2026-03-13T14:12:15+01:00","message":"(feat) O3-5364: Add configurable minimum age for displaying BMI (#2914)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Oliver Lewandowski","authorEmail":"109145288+olewandowski1@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"b2270525c8afea42e924e28916c44fa398fef91c","date":"2026-03-09T18:30:10+03:00","message":"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty\n\nJavaScript treats 0 as falsy, which caused zero-valued vitals to be\nsilently skipped across the entire pipeline — fetching, display,\nflagging, validation, and persistence.\n\nReplace all truthiness checks (if (value), Boolean(value), value && ...)\nwith explicit null checks (value != null && value !== '') so that 0 is\ntreated as a real recorded value while undefined, null, and empty strings\ncontinue to mean \"no value\".\n\nAffected layers:\n- assessValue: 0 is now evaluated against reference ranges and flagged\n- prepareObsForSubmission: 0-valued obs are created; editing to 0 no\n  longer voids the old obs without creating a replacement\n- data.resource: 0-valued FHIR observations are no longer dropped from\n  the encounter hash table\n- VitalsHeaderItem: 0 displays with its unit instead of \"Not available\"\n- vitals-header.extension: unit symbols render for 0-valued vitals\n- Form workspace: interpretation and range validation run for 0 values\n- Schema: a form with only a 0-valued field passes \"at least one field\"\n- Input validity: typing 0 is no longer flagged as invalid input\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback: null-check range thresholds and MUAC conditional\n\n- assessValue: use != null for range threshold checks (hiCritical,\n  hiNormal, lowCritical, lowNormal) so a threshold of 0 is not skipped\n- vitals header: use != null for MUAC conditional rendering for\n  consistency with the rest of the patch","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"8cfa2c6f1c106c7fac951b58ada21ad401e08b98","date":"2026-02-25T12:07:29+03:00","message":"(fix) Handle missing visit context in Angular form engine for visitless encounters (#3057)","refs":"","body":"The Angular form engine used `getPropOrThrow` for visit-related properties\n(`visitTypeUuid` and `visitUuid`) that are legitimately absent for\nvisitless encounters, causing it to crash with \"missing required Single\nSPA property\".\n\nThis was exposed by ebb3f1156 which correctly stopped falling back to\nthe active visit context when editing encounters, surfacing these latent\nbugs.\n\n- Pass visit context and patient from mapped encounter data to the form\n  widget slot in the encounters table\n- Change `getPropOrThrow` to `getProp` for `visitTypeUuid` in\n  `form-creation.service.ts` (wireDataSources)\n- Change `getPropOrThrow` to `getProp` for `visitUuid` in\n  `form-creation.service.ts` (setUpPayloadProcessingInformation),\n  `fe-wrapper.component.ts` (validateEncounterDatetimeWithVisit), and\n  `form-submission.service.ts` (submitEncounter)\n- Rename deprecated `browserTarget` to `buildTarget` in `angular.json`\n- Add tests for both visit-associated and visitless encounter scenarios","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"efc6d8f527acc021de816ff8f85d7015a0b48137","date":"2026-02-24T17:29:38+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows (#3050)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows\n\nReplace window.location.reload() with targeted SWR cache invalidation in both the mark-deceased form and mark-alive modal. After toggling death status, the patient data, current visit, and visit/encounter caches are revalidated so the UI updates reactively without a full page reload.\n\nAlso adds death date validation against the patient's date of birth: the date picker now sets minDate to the patient's birth date, and a Zod refine rejects death dates before DOB. The backend already has this check in PersonValidator, but the frontend was not enforcing it, allowing the user to submit and get a generic error toast.\n\nUpdates the warning text from \"will end any active visits\" to \"updates this patient's death information\" since the current /person endpoint does not actually close visits.\n\n* Update markDeceasedWarning translation to match component","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"97639b3a66fb0758e4a22cfb2a2ab64b3aaa2f38","date":"2026-02-11T22:59:01+03:00","message":"(fix) Derive unsaved changes from dirtyFields instead of isDirty in visit notes form (#3013)","refs":"","body":"Apply the same fix as the vitals form: use `dirtyFields` instead of\n`isDirty` for Save button disabled state and the `hasUnsavedChanges` workspace\nprop.\n\nReact Hook Form's form-level `isDirty` can be true when no field is\ndirty, causing false unsaved changes and enabling Save when the form is\nempty.\n\n- Add hasUserUnsavedChanges = Object.keys(dirtyFields).length > 0\n- Use it for button disabled and hasUnsavedChanges prop\n- Remove debug <pre>dirtyFields</pre> output\n- Test: type in clinical note before first submit so form is dirty and\n  validation runs (Save is now disabled when empty)","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d475445f57f7c7c6636c37caca373d0bed740511","date":"2026-02-05T16:28:35-05:00","message":"(fix) O3-5407 default the encounterDatetime of order basket submissio… (#2997)","refs":"","body":"(fix) O3-5407 default the encounterDatetime of order basket submission to server's current time\n\nCo-authored-by: Chi Bong Ho <hello@chibongho.net>","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"7c4d6a30f5821f51ef3b10088600591cdfd93b51","date":"2026-01-24T00:36:55+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5322: Submit multiple orders in parallel (#2946)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"BlessedAmrita","authorEmail":"153388147+BlessedAmrita@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"e952a6b8468040c64b77fccaeeaa7d1b3c2874a9","date":"2026-01-09T12:36:04-05:00","message":"(feat) O3-5304 add orderer and ordering location fields to order basket (#2920)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5304 add orderer and ordering location fields to order basket\n\n* address feedback\n\n* disable order basket submit button if orderer or order location not selected\n\n* Update e2e/specs/clinical-forms.spec.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"a54ee18edf3e20ce91dee366c708794e027693ef","date":"2025-11-26T12:40:05+03:00","message":"(test) Add coverage for optional primary diagnosis and improve config documentation","refs":"","body":"Test changes:\n- Add tests for `isPrimaryDiagnosisRequired` configuration behavior\n- Test visit note submission without diagnosis when config is false\n- Test validation enforcement when config is true\n- Remove unused `errorMessage` variable\n\nConfig improvements:\n- Add missing descriptions for all visit note config properties\n- Fix `formConceptUuid` type from `ConceptUuid` to `UUID`\n- Improve `diagnosisConceptClass` description for clarity\n\nRelated to #2836\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":69}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"adbc3248-1d37-4043-ac7c-81a7e0c5d543","uuid":"a17f1728-cac9-4f85-ab25-8acfdf408619","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:55:10.086Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"0731e41bea875494f9532b3ce882f7989f05ce07","date":"2026-10-06T15:24:43+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6044: Provide WHO z-score reference data to the Angular form engine (#3753)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-6044: Provide WHO z-score reference data to the Angular form engine\n\nesm-form-entry-app now registers the WHO reference data that the\nngx-formentry z-score helpers expect, so forms that calculate growth\nz-scores can be saved.\n\nThe helpers take the reference data as their first argument, e.g.\ncalcWeightForHeightZscore(weightForHeightRef, height, weight). The app\nnever registered weightForHeightRef, heightForAgeRef or bmiForAgeRef, so\nthese expressions failed as soon as a height or weight was entered. When\nan expression fails, the expression runner sets the field to false, and\nthe backend rejects false as the value of a numeric obs.\n\nwireDataSources now registers each reference the form schema mentions,\nwith the data for the patient's sex and age, chosen the same way as\nAMPATH's ng2-amrs. A reference that doesn't apply to the patient is\nregistered as null, which the helpers handle. The eight tables are\ncopied from esm-form-engine-lib and are identical to ng2-amrs's copies.\nEach one is a dynamic import, so forms that don't use the references\ndon't download them, and forms that do load at most two tables.\n\n* Use WHO's girls' height-for-age data and cover the month after age 5\n\nhfa_girls_5_above.json was a copy of the boys' table, so girls aged 5 to\n17 got height-for-age z-scores against boys' heights. It's now generated\nfrom WHO's Growth Reference 2007 girls' height-for-age z-score tables.\nEach column is M * (1 + k * S), rounded half to even to three decimals.\nThe same method regenerates hfa_boys_5_above.json byte for byte from\nWHO's boys' tables.\n\nThe loader switched to the 5 to 19 year tables on the fifth birthday,\nbut those start at 61 months, so height-for-age and BMI-for-age had no\nreference for a month. Height-for-age now uses the under-5 table through\nday 1,856, where that table ends, and the 5 to 19 year table from month\n61 after that. BMI-for-age has no under-5 table, so it has no reference\nuntil the 5 to 19 year table starts.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6ce8da22e588bfb7ee479298811f2bb4a064e2be","date":"2026-10-06T13:18:13+03:00","message":"(chore) O3-6025: Add missing form engine translation keys (#3754)","refs":"","body":"Adds the translation keys that the patient chart's form engine lib build\nuses but that weren't in esm-form-engine-app's key list, so they're\nextracted to en.json and can be translated. Until now these strings\nshowed in English in every locale.\n\nThree come from openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib#824, for the error shown when\na form's data fails to load: errorLoadingFormDependencies,\nretryLoadingFormDependencies and retry.\n\nThe other eight were added to the lib earlier and never listed: the\n\"Form submitted\" and \"Record updated\" toasts (submittedForm,\nsubmittedFormDescription, updatedRecord, updatedRecordDescription), the\nform submission error (errorProcessingFormSubmission), the mark-deceased\naction error (errorMarkingAsDeceased), and person attribute saving\n(personAttributesSaved, errorSavingPersonAttributes).\n\nen.json is regenerated with extract-translations. Every static t() key in\nthe lib build (4.2.2-pre.2663) is now in en.json.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"715ec982cb5008f64cf590e3335001b4de19843e","date":"2026-09-29T22:25:43+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry\n\nSave lab results and discontinue the test order in a single encounter\nrequest, then mark the order as fulfilled. The backend saves inline\norders inside the same transaction as the obs, so a failed discontinue\nno longer leaves the results saved behind it.\n\nPreviously the results, the discontinue and the fulfiller update were\nthree separate requests. If a later one failed, the results were already\nsaved, the order was not COMPLETED, and the form stayed in create mode.\nRetrying posted the obs to the encounter again. If the fulfiller update\nwas the one that failed, every retry added another copy and then failed\non the discontinue, because the backend rejects stopping an order twice.\n\nWhen an order already has saved results but is not COMPLETED, the form\nnow fills in the saved values and saving updates those obs. It then\ndiscontinues the order only if it is still active and marks it as\nfulfilled. A failed save refetches the saved results so the next attempt\nsees them.\n\n* Check for saved results when the user saves\n\nDecide whether to create or update results from a fresh fetch of the\norder's encounter at submit time, instead of the results the form loaded\nearlier. After a failed attempt, the form refetches its results in the\nbackground, and Save is available again before that refetch finishes.\nA quick retry in that window used to take the create path again. If the\nfetch fails, nothing is saved.\n\n* Keep the user's edits when saved results load\n\nOnly fill in saved result values for fields the user hasn't changed.\nAfter a failed save, the form refetches the saved results, and if the\nuser corrected a value while that was in flight, the refetched value\nreplaced their correction.\n\n* test: verify lab result edits are saved after delayed refresh\n\nExtend the delayed-results regression test through Save and close. Check that the corrected value is submitted, the workspace closes, and the success message is shown.\n\n* Cover failed lab result updates on retry\n\nCheck that a failed result update keeps the workspace open and stops the order from being completed. Update the refetch comment to describe how it fills in saved values.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"dd5d6a1d101e2647496fa4e5218ac4b7381d661c","date":"2026-09-25T06:53:36-04:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove support for offline from patient-chart (#3689)","refs":"","body":"Remove offline form submission, synchronization handlers, and offline visit helpers in preparation for removing offline support from the framework. Remove the related configuration, routes, and unused imports. This removes the offline visit API exported by patient-common-lib.","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"385d75cc2bbcc2a6802ca4f96dde611072cd4dec","date":"2026-09-17T21:05:49+03:00","message":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)","refs":"","body":"* fix: preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls\n\nTrack image additions and removals as form changes and read the current images for each upload callback so batches retain every file. Use labelled, contrasting remove buttons that do not submit the form. Cover create and edit workflows, batch uploads and removal.\n\n* fix: preserve image remove button contrast across interaction states\n\nSet explicit hover, focus and active colours so Carbon secondary button styles cannot hide the close icon. Remove the redundant button type, which Carbon already defaults to button.\n\n* fix: identify images in visit note removal labels\n\nUse the image description, filename or image number in each remove button's accessible name. Update the translation and tests to cover the fallbacks and select the intended image by name.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b147fb5906f1c3df18f12e3c804daeea486813d2","date":"2026-06-22T16:41:48+05:30","message":"(fix) Attach visit to visit note submissions (#3406)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"6797e139e35959962c51b4148213d88ccdc94af7","date":"2026-05-26T19:38:03+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5077: Support recording clinical procedures (#3320)","refs":"","body":"* Update pull request branches in CI workflow\n\nRemove main branch restriction from pull requests.\n\n* Remove 'patch/*' branch from CI trigger\n\n* Update CI workflow to include additional branches\n\n* Add esm-patient-procedures-app to patient-chart monorepo\n\n* Refactor the file structure\n\n* Add feat/procedure-history branch to workflow triggers\n\n* Modify E2E test triggers for additional branches\n\nUpdated branch filters for E2E tests on push and pull request events.\n\n* Make concept sources configurable\n\n* Load durations dynamically\n\n* Make the form wider\n\n* Make the duration unit combo box\n\n* Make status a combo box\n\n* (fix) O3-5656: Make submit buttons sticky on procedure history form (#3290)\n\n* Fix: stick the submit buttons in procedure form\n\n* Fix: update procedures-form.workspace.test.tsx to new ComboBox components\n\n* (fix) O3-5657: Various fixes to the procedures form (#3297)\n\n* (fix) O3-5653: Wire body site and status concepts in config schema (#3313)\n\n\n\nCo-authored-by: Jayasanka Weerasinghe <33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Cleanup the file structure\n\n* Migrate to vitest\n\n* Fix the workspace\n\n* Isolate date time component\n\n* Prevent future 'any' types\n\n* Convert all function declarations to arrow functions\n\n* Fix accessibility issues in ConceptSearchField (#15)\n\n* Clear slected concep when changing value\n\n* Re-enable delete button after failed delete\n\nsetIsDeleting(false) was missing from the catch block, leaving\nthe Delete button permanently disabled after a transient error.\nUser had to close and reopen the modal to retry.\n\nAlso updates the test assertion to verify the button is re-enabled\nafter an error so the user can retry without reopening the modal.\n\n* docs: add README for esm-patient-procedures-app\n\n* Add README for esm-patient-procedures-app\n\n* Rename file\n\n* Enable delete button on error\n\n* Rename file\n\n* Add separate pagination configs for overview and detailed view\n\n* Align import order and type placement with O3 coding conventions\n\n* Add unit tests for ConceptSearchField and ProceduresActionMenu (#21)\n\n* Add test cases for procedures form component\n\n* Rename close workspace\n\n* Add translations to zod schema\n\n* Minor cleanups\n\n* Reset workflows\n\n* Remove unused abort controller\n\n* Update routes\n\n* Fix the overvierw URL\n\n* Add backend dependancies\n\n* fix: convert type-only imports to 'import type' syntax in procedures-app\n\nConvert all type-only imports in the procedures-app package to use\nthe 'import type' syntax instead of inline 'type' prefixes. This\nimproves code consistency and clarity.\n\nUpdated files:\n- procedures.resource.ts\n- dashboard.meta.ts\n- components/**/*.tsx\n- workspaces/procedures-form/**/*.tsx\n\nAddressed in PR #3320 review comment.\n\n* Remove selectedConcept from hook, use RHF as UUID source of truth\n\n* Surface hook errors in the UI\n\n* Address remaining PR review comments from denniskigen\n\n* Set date boundaries\n\n* Update config descriptions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dilan Kavishka <109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","authorEmail":"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2c514a99a75389e9ccf680a9584eb68db57a2267","date":"2026-04-21T16:48:02+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5618: Validate condition selection before submit triggers (#3240)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Om Srivastava","authorEmail":"79087911+omsrivastava512@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d4857fbf84af21943b989c91c1b37277ff3ff2fd","date":"2026-04-17T16:01:13+03:00","message":"(feat) Surface BMI reference ranges in the biometrics table (#3238)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1ea865ec269e781482352f0307b124b2b78443aa","date":"2026-03-23T22:39:28+03:00","message":"(fix) Return promises from onSubmit handlers to track isSubmitting (#3158)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"05fb7434b9c74c51773439a5f94580ab7651b91d","date":"2026-03-23T23:22:32+05:30","message":"(fix) Prevent duplicate encounter creation on repeated submit (#3156)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Om Srivastava","authorEmail":"79087911+omsrivastava512@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"3e58d3eb4e079c4d530e105dcd963f034e4f9271","date":"2026-03-13T14:12:15+01:00","message":"(feat) O3-5364: Add configurable minimum age for displaying BMI (#2914)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Oliver Lewandowski","authorEmail":"109145288+olewandowski1@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"b2270525c8afea42e924e28916c44fa398fef91c","date":"2026-03-09T18:30:10+03:00","message":"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty\n\nJavaScript treats 0 as falsy, which caused zero-valued vitals to be\nsilently skipped across the entire pipeline — fetching, display,\nflagging, validation, and persistence.\n\nReplace all truthiness checks (if (value), Boolean(value), value && ...)\nwith explicit null checks (value != null && value !== '') so that 0 is\ntreated as a real recorded value while undefined, null, and empty strings\ncontinue to mean \"no value\".\n\nAffected layers:\n- assessValue: 0 is now evaluated against reference ranges and flagged\n- prepareObsForSubmission: 0-valued obs are created; editing to 0 no\n  longer voids the old obs without creating a replacement\n- data.resource: 0-valued FHIR observations are no longer dropped from\n  the encounter hash table\n- VitalsHeaderItem: 0 displays with its unit instead of \"Not available\"\n- vitals-header.extension: unit symbols render for 0-valued vitals\n- Form workspace: interpretation and range validation run for 0 values\n- Schema: a form with only a 0-valued field passes \"at least one field\"\n- Input validity: typing 0 is no longer flagged as invalid input\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback: null-check range thresholds and MUAC conditional\n\n- assessValue: use != null for range threshold checks (hiCritical,\n  hiNormal, lowCritical, lowNormal) so a threshold of 0 is not skipped\n- vitals header: use != null for MUAC conditional rendering for\n  consistency with the rest of the patch","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"8cfa2c6f1c106c7fac951b58ada21ad401e08b98","date":"2026-02-25T12:07:29+03:00","message":"(fix) Handle missing visit context in Angular form engine for visitless encounters (#3057)","refs":"","body":"The Angular form engine used `getPropOrThrow` for visit-related properties\n(`visitTypeUuid` and `visitUuid`) that are legitimately absent for\nvisitless encounters, causing it to crash with \"missing required Single\nSPA property\".\n\nThis was exposed by ebb3f1156 which correctly stopped falling back to\nthe active visit context when editing encounters, surfacing these latent\nbugs.\n\n- Pass visit context and patient from mapped encounter data to the form\n  widget slot in the encounters table\n- Change `getPropOrThrow` to `getProp` for `visitTypeUuid` in\n  `form-creation.service.ts` (wireDataSources)\n- Change `getPropOrThrow` to `getProp` for `visitUuid` in\n  `form-creation.service.ts` (setUpPayloadProcessingInformation),\n  `fe-wrapper.component.ts` (validateEncounterDatetimeWithVisit), and\n  `form-submission.service.ts` (submitEncounter)\n- Rename deprecated `browserTarget` to `buildTarget` in `angular.json`\n- Add tests for both visit-associated and visitless encounter scenarios","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"efc6d8f527acc021de816ff8f85d7015a0b48137","date":"2026-02-24T17:29:38+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows (#3050)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows\n\nReplace window.location.reload() with targeted SWR cache invalidation in both the mark-deceased form and mark-alive modal. After toggling death status, the patient data, current visit, and visit/encounter caches are revalidated so the UI updates reactively without a full page reload.\n\nAlso adds death date validation against the patient's date of birth: the date picker now sets minDate to the patient's birth date, and a Zod refine rejects death dates before DOB. The backend already has this check in PersonValidator, but the frontend was not enforcing it, allowing the user to submit and get a generic error toast.\n\nUpdates the warning text from \"will end any active visits\" to \"updates this patient's death information\" since the current /person endpoint does not actually close visits.\n\n* Update markDeceasedWarning translation to match component","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"97639b3a66fb0758e4a22cfb2a2ab64b3aaa2f38","date":"2026-02-11T22:59:01+03:00","message":"(fix) Derive unsaved changes from dirtyFields instead of isDirty in visit notes form (#3013)","refs":"","body":"Apply the same fix as the vitals form: use `dirtyFields` instead of\n`isDirty` for Save button disabled state and the `hasUnsavedChanges` workspace\nprop.\n\nReact Hook Form's form-level `isDirty` can be true when no field is\ndirty, causing false unsaved changes and enabling Save when the form is\nempty.\n\n- Add hasUserUnsavedChanges = Object.keys(dirtyFields).length > 0\n- Use it for button disabled and hasUnsavedChanges prop\n- Remove debug <pre>dirtyFields</pre> output\n- Test: type in clinical note before first submit so form is dirty and\n  validation runs (Save is now disabled when empty)","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d475445f57f7c7c6636c37caca373d0bed740511","date":"2026-02-05T16:28:35-05:00","message":"(fix) O3-5407 default the encounterDatetime of order basket submissio… (#2997)","refs":"","body":"(fix) O3-5407 default the encounterDatetime of order basket submission to server's current time\n\nCo-authored-by: Chi Bong Ho <hello@chibongho.net>","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"7c4d6a30f5821f51ef3b10088600591cdfd93b51","date":"2026-01-24T00:36:55+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5322: Submit multiple orders in parallel (#2946)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"BlessedAmrita","authorEmail":"153388147+BlessedAmrita@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"e952a6b8468040c64b77fccaeeaa7d1b3c2874a9","date":"2026-01-09T12:36:04-05:00","message":"(feat) O3-5304 add orderer and ordering location fields to order basket (#2920)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5304 add orderer and ordering location fields to order basket\n\n* address feedback\n\n* disable order basket submit button if orderer or order location not selected\n\n* Update e2e/specs/clinical-forms.spec.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"a54ee18edf3e20ce91dee366c708794e027693ef","date":"2025-11-26T12:40:05+03:00","message":"(test) Add coverage for optional primary diagnosis and improve config documentation","refs":"","body":"Test changes:\n- Add tests for `isPrimaryDiagnosisRequired` configuration behavior\n- Test visit note submission without diagnosis when config is false\n- Test validation enforcement when config is true\n- Remove unused `errorMessage` variable\n\nConfig improvements:\n- Add missing descriptions for all visit note config properties\n- Fix `formConceptUuid` type from `ConceptUuid` to `UUID`\n- Improve `diagnosisConceptClass` description for clarity\n\nRelated to #2836\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":69}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Dn51wfiLxrD5YJeM195oa6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
