{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012EJjLUWokiUFcAG37yqRbG","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"0e06523b799319ec65716df66eafb32aef170b3c","date":"2026-10-13T12:37:47+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6100: Prevent duplicate vitals saves (#3792)","refs":"","body":"Return the save promise so the form keeps Save and close disabled until\nthe request finishes. This prevents a double-click from saving the same\nmeasurements twice.\n\nAdd coverage for double-clicking Save and close during a pending request\nand retrying a failed save without losing the entered measurements.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d4857fbf84af21943b989c91c1b37277ff3ff2fd","date":"2026-04-17T16:01:13+03:00","message":"(feat) Surface BMI reference ranges in the biometrics table (#3238)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"3e58d3eb4e079c4d530e105dcd963f034e4f9271","date":"2026-03-13T14:12:15+01:00","message":"(feat) O3-5364: Add configurable minimum age for displaying BMI (#2914)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Oliver Lewandowski","authorEmail":"109145288+olewandowski1@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"b2270525c8afea42e924e28916c44fa398fef91c","date":"2026-03-09T18:30:10+03:00","message":"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty\n\nJavaScript treats 0 as falsy, which caused zero-valued vitals to be\nsilently skipped across the entire pipeline — fetching, display,\nflagging, validation, and persistence.\n\nReplace all truthiness checks (if (value), Boolean(value), value && ...)\nwith explicit null checks (value != null && value !== '') so that 0 is\ntreated as a real recorded value while undefined, null, and empty strings\ncontinue to mean \"no value\".\n\nAffected layers:\n- assessValue: 0 is now evaluated against reference ranges and flagged\n- prepareObsForSubmission: 0-valued obs are created; editing to 0 no\n  longer voids the old obs without creating a replacement\n- data.resource: 0-valued FHIR observations are no longer dropped from\n  the encounter hash table\n- VitalsHeaderItem: 0 displays with its unit instead of \"Not available\"\n- vitals-header.extension: unit symbols render for 0-valued vitals\n- Form workspace: interpretation and range validation run for 0 values\n- Schema: a form with only a 0-valued field passes \"at least one field\"\n- Input validity: typing 0 is no longer flagged as invalid input\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback: null-check range thresholds and MUAC conditional\n\n- assessValue: use != null for range threshold checks (hiCritical,\n  hiNormal, lowCritical, lowNormal) so a threshold of 0 is not skipped\n- vitals header: use != null for MUAC conditional rendering for\n  consistency with the rest of the patch","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"0599558fdb8e2c2ab990f688b8f019f1559187da","date":"2026-02-11T22:23:50+03:00","message":"(fix) Derive unsaved changes from dirtyFields instead of isDirty in vitals form (#3012)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"9465b6b181bd8e5385cf418b09fcf7a172a1d590","date":"2026-01-05T17:45:17+03:00","message":"(chore) Upgrade TypeScript ESLint to v8 and fix type issues (#2913)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1cae1653b6f2aa4435310ac356e4170778eb64d0","date":"2025-12-04T08:57:33-05:00","message":"(BREAKING) O3-4961 Workspace v2 migration (#2800)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-4962 store visitContext in patient chart store\n\n* fix immunization-from test failure\n\n* add missing changes\n\n* add e2e test for visit context\n\n* clear visit context when ending or deleting active visit\n\n* migrate visit-context-switcher to use patinet chart store\n\n* fix visit context unset incorrectly when ending active visit\n\n* (BREAKING) Workspace v2 migration\n\n* address PR feedback\n\n* add e2e test steps for visit context when deleting and restoring active visit\n\n* fix unit tests\n\n* fix e2e tests\n\n* update esm-core and fix order basket\n\n* add exported workspaces\n\n* remove unused cancel-order-form\n\n* exported workspaces fixup\n\n* comments\n\n* migrate fill-prescription form workspace\n\n* fix NPE\n\n* fix e2e tests\n\n* address feedback\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-medications-app/src/routes.json\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"}],"totalCount":7}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"adbc3248-1d37-4043-ac7c-81a7e0c5d543","uuid":"18383614-8629-4d22-9478-48e3c574f087","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:55:23.196Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"0e06523b799319ec65716df66eafb32aef170b3c","date":"2026-10-13T12:37:47+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6100: Prevent duplicate vitals saves (#3792)","refs":"","body":"Return the save promise so the form keeps Save and close disabled until\nthe request finishes. This prevents a double-click from saving the same\nmeasurements twice.\n\nAdd coverage for double-clicking Save and close during a pending request\nand retrying a failed save without losing the entered measurements.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d4857fbf84af21943b989c91c1b37277ff3ff2fd","date":"2026-04-17T16:01:13+03:00","message":"(feat) Surface BMI reference ranges in the biometrics table (#3238)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"3e58d3eb4e079c4d530e105dcd963f034e4f9271","date":"2026-03-13T14:12:15+01:00","message":"(feat) O3-5364: Add configurable minimum age for displaying BMI (#2914)","refs":"","body":"","a